    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "We have two different widgets that consume the metadata declared by other widgets: `Reset` and `CurrentFilters`.\n- `CurrentFilters` displays filters from `RefinementList`, `Menu`, `Toggle`, etc. However, it doesn't display the current query nor the current page. And when you click on its `Clear All` button, it doesn't clear them either.\n- `Reset` clears _everything_.\n\nAs such, I've made a distinction between two types of filters: visible filters (that are displayed in `CurrentFilters`) and invisible filters, that aren't displayed nor cleared by `CurrentFilters` but that are correctly cleared by `Reset`. Invisible filters are declared by setting the `hide` property to `true` on a filter object.\n",
    "commit_id": "0609244f5a883922e4e863e9acba8179e0b6148c",
